        "instanceType": "StudyAmendment",
        "summary": "This amendment is considered to be substantial because it is likely to have a significant impact on the safety or the rights of the study participants. Changes include: replacement of \"mucosal healing\" with \"histologic-endoscopic mucosal improvement plus absence of neutrophils\" per regulatory feedback; clarification of lifestyle goals in the Schedule of Activities; correction of hematology and clinical chemistry testing for Visit 7; deletion of mMS review at Visits 8, 15, and ED; addition of risk assessment for gallbladder disease in tirzepatide; correction of exploratory endpoint for visceral fat measurement; addition of colorectal cancer surveillance wording to inclusion criteria; removal of duplicate text from inclusion criteria; clarifications to exclusion criteria; addition of ECG exclusion criterion per regulatory feedback; additional details for continued access to study interventions; and correction of FDA guidance reference year.",
        "effectiveDate": "2025-11-04",
